WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.960
Welcome to the Microsoft for Education Daily, Wednesday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.180
Here's your day in Microsoft updates, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.840
Your class, your rules. Teachers can now assign Copilot's Study and Learn,

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.990
right inside a Teams assignment.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.720
You set the AI rule: allowed, editing or brainstorming only, or none.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.880
Study and Learn reads the assignment, its instructions and files,

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.910
then coaches with questions, hints and feedback.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.960
Students can turn it into a practice quiz,

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:46.020
flashcards or a matching activity, and it stays in tutoring mode.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:53.690
For students 13 and up, on A1, A3 or A5. IT enables it for under-18s.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:57.920
And Microsoft Classroom hit the roadmap: preview next February,

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.700
rollout starting next June.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.090
For school IT, Windows administrator protection is now generally available.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.200
Admins run as standard users. When a task needs more,

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.990
Windows Hello approves that task alone.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.130
Coding students can now pick MAI Code 2 Flash,

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:21.810
Microsoft's new lightweight model, in GitHub Copilot.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.730
And database students can run Azure SQL Database on a laptop,

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:29.500
in preview, with no Azure subscription.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.570
Got Microsoft 365 Copilot? Word,

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:37.380
Excel and PowerPoint now work right inside the Copilot app.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.560
In South Africa,

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:44.330
CAPEability AI brings AI and job skills to the Western Cape's libraries and e-Centres.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.620
The fine print? Windows PowerShell 5.1 is deprecated,

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:51.410
though it's still supported and patched.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.130
The next Windows brings PowerShell 7,

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:58.820
so check which scripts still launch powershell.exe.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.770
After hours,

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:08.760
Copilot on Copilot+ PCs will soon run a read-only scan to explain what's wrong.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:12.180
And it'll tidy a messy Downloads folder,

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:15.560
finding, moving or renaming files when you ask.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:20.140
Oh, and on December 1, Game Pass adds Hela,

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:23.860
a co-op adventure starring a brave little mouse.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.050
However much AI arrives this week, it's still your class, your rules.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.820
Every day, the changelog gets a little longer.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.620
Some of it's shipped. The rest is on its way.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.880
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.950
That's the Microsoft for Education Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.940
See you tomorrow.
